# XSH posix_spawnattr_getsigmask() and posix_spawnattr_setsigmask()
# Copyright (c) 2026 Nicholas Martin. All rights reserved.
#
# Effects are shown by really spawning this program as a child image. The
# functions return the error number; errno is not used. SIGKILL and SIGSTOP
# are not put in sets.

assertion  XSH.posix_spawnattr_getsigmask.001
anchor     functions/posix_spawnattr_getsigmask.html#RETURN VALUE
anchor     functions/posix_spawnattr_getsigmask.html#DESCRIPTION
class      required
since      2001
says       posix_spawnattr_getsigmask() on a newly initialised object returns 0
           (the set stored is unspecified and not examined).
test       t/001-default.c

assertion  XSH.posix_spawnattr_getsigmask.002
anchor     functions/posix_spawnattr_getsigmask.html#DESCRIPTION
anchor     functions/posix_spawnattr_getsigmask.html#RETURN VALUE
class      required
since      2001
says       posix_spawnattr_setsigmask() with a set of SIGUSR1, SIGTERM and SIGRTMIN
           returns 0 and posix_spawnattr_getsigmask() returns 0 and
           stores exactly that set; a second object keeps its own
           different set.
test       t/002-roundtrip.c

assertion  XSH.posix_spawnattr_getsigmask.003
anchor     functions/posix_spawnattr_getsigmask.html#DESCRIPTION
class      required
since      2001
says       A later posix_spawnattr_setsigmask() replaces the set (an empty set
           after a non-empty one reads back empty), and the attribute is
           a copy: changing the caller's set variable after the call
           does not change what is read back.
test       t/003-replace-copy.c

assertion  XSH.posix_spawnattr_getsigmask.004
anchor     functions/posix_spawnattr_getsigmask.html#DESCRIPTION
anchor     functions/posix_spawn.html#DESCRIPTION
class      required
since      2001
says       With POSIX_SPAWN_SETSIGMASK set and the spawn-sigmask set holding
           SIGUSR1, a child of a parent whose mask is empty has SIGUSR1
           blocked and SIGUSR2 not blocked, and the parent's own mask is
           unchanged.
test       t/004-effect.c
